ce mapping records a Lean proof of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.lem-skipped-endpoint-trichotomy"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.lem-skipped-endpoint-trichotomy"],"id":"long.lem-skipped-endpoint-trichotomy","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Lemma 6.45 (The signed position of a skipped greedy prefix)","locator":"Long record Lemma 6.45, p. 57, label lem:skipped-endpoint-trichotomy","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $s\\ge5$ be omitted by the real greedy support $G$, and put\n$$\nH_s=G\\cap\\{2,\\ldots,s-1\\},\\qquad\n f_s=\\sum_{d\\in H_s}\\left\\lfloor\\frac{4^s}{2^d-1}\\right\\rfloor-T_s.\n$$\nExactly one of the following holds:\n$$\n\\begin{array}{lll}\n f_s<0:& H_s=D_s,& f_s=-\\mathrm{rem}(s),\\quad \\mathrm{rem}(s)\\ge1;\\\\\n f_s=0:& H_s=D_s,& \\mathrm{rem}(s)=0;\\\\\n f_s>0:& H_s=B_s,& f_s=o_s.\n \\end{array}\n$$\nThus the real greedy prefix is one of the two adjacent integer words. This classifies its signed distance $f_s$ from $T_s$; it does not exclude the negative case. Nor does it identify $f_s$ with the different coordinate $C_s=4\\mathrm{rem}(s)-p_s^- -4$ used in the final-middle argument.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.lem-skipped-endpoint-trichotomy","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.lem-skipped-endpoint-trichotomy","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.lem-skipped-endpoint-trichotomy%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.halfGreedy_skipped_endpoint_trichotomy%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.lem-skipped-endpoint-trichotomy%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.halfGreedy_skipped_endpoint_trichotomy%22%2C%22formalizes%22